"""Editorial question designs for entrepreneurship, startups, and unicorn companies."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


ENTREPRENEURSHIP = """history_origins|A Local Business Formation Wave|Which conditions led people to start firms in one place?|Use dated registrations, jobs, credit, and market records.
famous_examples|A Founder Story Rechecked|Which resources and collaborators made a cited business possible?|Test capital, prior skills, timing, labor, and survivorship bias.
hidden_stories|Entrepreneurs Outside Headlines|Who starts small or informal enterprises and why?|Use defined population and consented accounts.
beginner_explainers|From Idea to Operating Business|What steps turned one proposal into sales?|Trace customer need, costs, permits, supply, and first transactions.
advanced_concepts|Opportunity and Constraint|How do financing, care, and market access shape who can start?|Compare matched groups and local institutions.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why a New Firm Did Not Grow|Which records distinguish demand, capital, and capacity limits?|Use dated books, customer data, and founder accounts.
technology_innovation|A Tool for Small Firms|Did one technology change productivity or reach?|Compare adoption cost, labor, sales, and alternatives.
people_personalities|A Founder and Their Team|Which decisions can be attributed to a named founder?|Use records and employee or partner perspectives.
major_events|A Shock to New Businesses|How did one policy or crisis affect formation?|Compare entry, exits, sectors, and counterfactual limits.
how_it_works|A Business's First Year|How do sales, inventory, cash, taxes, and wages interact?|Follow a consented case with clear accounting periods.
rise_fall|Business Births and Closures|What explains a measured change in one market?|Define enterprise birth, exit, survival, and geography.
then_vs_now|Starting a Firm in Two Periods|How did costs, rules, and channels change?|Use matched sector and jurisdiction.
future_developments|Conditions for More Entry|Which changes could widen viable business creation?|State capital, demand, infrastructure, and policy assumptions.
myths_vs_facts|Anyone Can Bootstrap?|What resources did successful cases actually use?|Include savings, unpaid labor, networks, and credit.
documentary_stories|One Business from Plan to Sale|What happened between market test and first repeat customer?|Use dated records and consented interviews.
value_chain|A New Firm's Place|Which suppliers and distributors must it rely on?|Map contracts, margins, and dependency.
incentive_map|Who Shares the Upside|How do founder, worker, lender, partner, and customer interests differ?|Use ownership and contract terms.
unit_economics|Does Each Sale Help|What remains after variable costs?|Define unit, channel, returns, labor, and period.
consumer_outcome|Did the New Firm Solve a Problem|What did customers receive at what total cost?|Compare alternatives, quality, access, and repeat use.
market_structure|Can a New Entrant Compete|Which incumbents and substitutes constrain it?|Define market, geography, and entry barriers.
risk_transfer|Who Carries Startup Risk|How are losses shared among household, workers, lenders, and suppliers?|Trace guarantees, pay, credit, and failure terms.
regulatory_choice|A Rule and New Entrants|Did one licensing change alter formation?|Name jurisdiction and date; test outcomes and enforcement.
historical_shock|Starting During a Downturn|Which firms entered and survived?|Use cohort definitions, financing, and demand evidence.
data_definition|Who Counts as an Entrepreneur|How do self-employment, ownership, and enterprise births differ?|Specify dataset, worker status, and informal activity.
access_and_affordability|Who Can Afford to Start|Which capital and service barriers vary across groups?|Use costs, credit terms, care needs, and local context.
business_failure|A Closure Without Myth|What evidence explains one firm's exit?|Separate insolvency, sale, retirement, and voluntary closure.
long_term_tradeoff|Growth or Stability|How do founders weigh expansion against income and control?|Use consented goals and financial constraints.
field_supply_chain|First Supplier Contract|Which terms shape a small firm's reliability?|Check minimums, lead times, payment, and substitutes.
field_brand_claims|An Origin Story Audited|Which claims about founder or product are documented?|Compare marketing with dated records.
field_customer_experience|A First Purchase|Where do customer expectations match delivery?|Observe consentfully from search to support.
field_market_entry|Opening in One Place|What practical costs and permissions are required?|Use current local sources; avoid generic legal advice.
field_product_lifecycle|A Product's Early Revisions|How did customer evidence change the offer?|Trace versions, costs, and usage.
"""

STARTUPS = """history_origins|How One Startup Was Founded|What customer problem and resources shaped its first version?|Use dated pitches, product records, and team accounts.
famous_examples|A Startup Success Rechecked|Which metrics support its reputation?|Separate users, revenue, margin, cash flow, and valuation.
hidden_stories|The Team Behind a Founder|Whose engineering, support, sales, and operations made growth possible?|Trace credits, equity, and labor.
beginner_explainers|Testing a Startup Hypothesis|What evidence shows a product solves a defined problem?|Compare interviews, experiments, usage, and paying customers.
advanced_concepts|Growth Versus Unit Economics|When can fast adoption still destroy value?|Model contribution margin, retention, acquisition, and burn.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Growth Stalled|Which data distinguish weak demand from execution failure?|Check cohorts, pricing, competitors, and product changes.
technology_innovation|A Claimed Technical Edge|Does a named feature create measurable advantage?|Compare baseline, performance, reliability, cost, and user outcomes.
people_personalities|A Founder Decision Under Pressure|What alternatives were available at a turning point?|Use board records, team accounts, funding, and outcome.
major_events|A Funding Round or Layoff|How did one event change the firm's plan?|Trace cash runway, staffing, product, and investor terms.
how_it_works|From Prototype to Repeat Use|What systems support a startup's product?|Map build, onboarding, payments, service, and support.
rise_fall|A Startup's Growth Curve|Which metric actually rose or fell?|Define cohort, period, channel, and denominator.
then_vs_now|Product Before and After Funding|What changed in service, cost, and customers?|Compare dated versions and financial records.
future_developments|Paths to Sustainable Operation|Which assumptions determine runway and scale?|State burn, revenue, retention, capital, and risk scenarios.
myths_vs_facts|Growth at Any Cost?|Did rapid spending improve durable customer value?|Compare cohort returns and full costs.
documentary_stories|One Startup Experiment|What was proposed, measured, learned, and changed?|Use dated experiment records; separate post-hoc narrative.
value_chain|The Startup's Dependencies|Which platforms, suppliers, and channels could stop it?|Map contracts, fees, and fallback options.
incentive_map|Equity and Control|How do founders, staff, investors, and customers differ?|Read cap table and governance terms where available.
unit_economics|One Customer Cohort|Does revenue cover acquisition and service?|Define cohort, churn, gross margin, payback, and assumptions.
consumer_outcome|Does the Product Help|What measurable outcome improved for users?|Compare baseline, harms, access, and alternatives.
market_structure|The Market Actually Served|Which customers and substitutes constrain growth?|Define segment and geography before total-addressable-market claims.
risk_transfer|Who Bears a Pivot|How do product changes affect employees, users, and suppliers?|Trace contracts, data, pay, and service obligations.
regulatory_choice|A Rule Facing a Startup|How did a dated rule alter the model?|Name jurisdiction, compliance cost, and observed response.
historical_shock|A Downturn and Runway|How did funding conditions affect the firm?|Compare burn, sales, layoffs, and financing terms.
data_definition|What Counts as a Startup|Is the case new, innovative, high-growth, or merely small?|State criterion, age, legal form, and source.
access_and_affordability|Who Can Use the Product|Does pricing or design exclude a group?|Test total price, accessibility, language, and support.
business_failure|An Exit or Shutdown|What happened to customers and workers?|Distinguish acquisition, insolvency, wind-down, and product closure.
long_term_tradeoff|Fast Scale Versus Reliability|What breaks when adoption outpaces support?|Compare outages, complaints, staff load, and retention.
field_supply_chain|An External API Dependency|How do pricing or terms expose the product?|Trace contract, usage, alternatives, and incident history.
field_brand_claims|Testing a Startup Promise|Which claims have measured evidence?|Check benchmark, sample, version, and exclusions.
field_customer_experience|First Week of Use|Where does onboarding succeed or fail?|Test consentfully across signup, core task, billing, and support.
field_market_entry|Finding First Customers|Which channel delivered repeat buyers?|Compare outreach cost, conversion, retention, and selection bias.
field_product_lifecycle|From Minimum Version to Current Product|What changed and why?|Trace releases, feedback, defects, and outcomes.
"""

UNICORN_COMPANIES = """history_origins|How a Firm Reached the Label|Which financing event produced a reported billion-dollar valuation?|Read dated terms and company stage.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Unicorn Rechecked|What did valuation say about revenue and profit?|Separate financing price, capitalization, cash flow, and uncertainty.
hidden_stories|Workers Behind a Valuation|How did growth affect employees and contractors?|Trace pay, equity, dilution, workload, and consented accounts.
beginner_explainers|What Unicorn Means|How is a private valuation inferred from a funding round?|Explain share class, price, dilution, and timing.
advanced_concepts|Preferred Shares and Headline Value|How can investor rights change the meaning of a quoted valuation?|Compare liquidation preference and common-share economics.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why a Valuation Changed|Which evidence explains an up-round or down-round?|Test performance, terms, market multiples, and financing pressure.
technology_innovation|The Claimed Moat|Which technical advantage remained durable?|Compare performance, cost, imitation, and customers.
people_personalities|The Financing Decision Makers|Who accepted a round and on what terms?|Use filings, board accounts, and investor materials.
major_events|A Down-Round or Public Listing|How did one event reveal a different market price?|Compare share classes, dates, lockups, and disclosures.
how_it_works|From Round to Headline Number|How does a funding price become a company valuation?|Trace fully diluted shares, class rights, and assumptions.
rise_fall|A Unicorn's Valuation Path|What changed in reported value over time?|Match round terms, currency, dilution, and reporting source.
then_vs_now|Private and Public Measures|How did reported value compare after listing?|Adjust for share count, rights, date, and market conditions.
future_developments|Conditional Paths to Exit|Which assumptions affect IPO, sale, or continued private funding?|State revenue, cash, market, and governance scenarios.
myths_vs_facts|Unicorn Means Profitable?|What do available records show about earnings and cash?|Distinguish absent disclosure from proof of loss or profit.
documentary_stories|One Financing Round Examined|What claims and rights accompanied the deal?|Build dated timeline from filings and reliable records.
value_chain|Where Value Is Captured|Which partners and platforms take part of each sale?|Map distribution, supplier, payments, and data dependencies.
incentive_map|Common Versus Preferred Holders|How do outcomes differ for founders, staff, and investors?|Model rights, dilution, and exit proceeds without advice.
unit_economics|Growth Behind the Price|Do customer cohorts cover acquisition and service costs?|Use defined margin, retention, and disclosed limits.
consumer_outcome|Customer Value Amid Growth|Did scale improve service or choice?|Compare price, quality, access, and complaints.
market_structure|A Unicorn's Actual Market|Does it dominate a defined segment?|Specify substitutes, geography, share, and data limits.
risk_transfer|Who Pays if Growth Stops|How do losses fall on staff, suppliers, customers, and owners?|Trace contracts, layoffs, credits, and equity terms.
regulatory_choice|Private Company Disclosure|Which jurisdictional rule affects reported information?|Name date and authority; distinguish requirement from voluntary claim.
historical_shock|Valuations During a Funding Cycle|How did market conditions affect rounds?|Compare financing terms and operating metrics across dates.
data_definition|Counting Unicorns|When is a firm included or removed from a list?|Define private status, currency, round date, and data source.
access_and_affordability|Does Scale Widen Access|Which customers gain or lose under the model?|Compare total price, availability, design, and subsidy.
business_failure|A Former Unicorn's Wind-Down|What happened to assets and obligations?|Use filings, workers, creditors, customers, and timeline.
long_term_tradeoff|Valuation Versus Durability|Can the firm sustain service without new capital?|Model cash, margins, retention, and financing assumptions.
field_supply_chain|A Critical Partner|Which supplier or platform underpins the model?|Check contract, concentration, cost, and alternatives.
field_brand_claims|A Billion-Dollar Story Audited|Which growth and innovation claims are verifiable?|Date each claim and distinguish forecast from result.
field_customer_experience|Service at Scale|What happens to a defined customer as volume grows?|Compare onboarding, reliability, support, and billing.
field_market_entry|A Rival to the Unicorn|Which barriers are inherent and which are contractual?|Test capital, network effects, distribution, and rules.
field_product_lifecycle|From Subsidized Offer to Mature Service|How did price and features change?|Trace versions, funding stages, and customer outcomes.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("302", "302_entrepreneurship", ENTREPRENEURSHIP,
                  "Entrepreneurship as formation and operation of varied new enterprises, including small and informal firms.",
                  "business demography definitions and data, dated registrations and financial records, current local requirements, and consented founder, worker, and customer accounts",
                  "Name market, jurisdiction, cohort, and period. Avoid founder hero stories, survivor-only samples, and generic legal or financing advice.")
    revise_domain("303", "303_startups", STARTUPS,
                  "Startups through testable product hypotheses, customer cohorts, unit economics, financing, team work, and service outcomes.",
                  "dated product versions and experiments, customer and financial cohorts, financing terms, incidents, and consented team and user accounts",
                  "Define what counts as a startup and name company, product, market, and period. Distinguish pitch claims from measured results and avoid investment advice.")
    revise_domain("304", "304_unicorn_companies", UNICORN_COMPANIES,
                  "Private-company unicorn labels through financing terms, reported valuations, operating results, workers, and customers.",
                  "dated financing and securities disclosures where available, company accounts, product and customer data, and consented worker and user accounts",
                  "Name company, valuation date, currency, share class, and data source. A financing valuation is not a verified market price for all shares or proof of profitability.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
